{"body":"\u003ca href=\"#\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e **Aliases bypass storage checks**\n\nWhen `install --path` is invoked through a Cargo alias, `manifest_in_scope` does not recognize it because path-install detection only matches the literal `install` subcommand. For example, running an alias such as `cargo i --path /project` outside a workspace returns from this branch before the existing alias-resolution logic runs, even though Cargo will compile `/project/Cargo.toml`. The build therefore bypasses the metadata and storage checks. Alias resolution must happen before applying this manifest-less passthrough, or this case must be rejected conservatively.\n\n**Knowledge Base Used:**\n- [Cargo cache integration](https://app.greptile.com/jdx-org/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/jdx/mr-boxington/-/docs/cargo-cache-integration.md)\n- [CLI and configuration](https://app.greptile.com/jdx-org/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/jdx/mr-boxington/-/docs/mbx-cli-and-config.md)\n\n\u003ca href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20crates%2Fmbx%2Fsrc%2Fcli%2Fshim.rs%0ALine%3A%20256-260%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Aliases%20bypass%20storage%20checks**%0A%0AWhen%20%60install%20--path%60%20is%20invoked%20through%20a%20Cargo%20alias%2C%20%60manifest_in_scope%60%20does%20not%20recognize%20it%20because%20path-install%20detection%20only%20matches%20the%20literal%20%60install%60%20subcommand.%20For%20example%2C%20running%20an%20alias%20such%20as%20%60cargo%20i%20--path%20%2Fproject%60%20outside%20a%20workspace%20returns%20from%20this%20branch%20before%20the%20existing%20alias-resolution%20logic%20runs%2C%20even%20though%20Cargo%20will%20compile%20%60%2Fproject%2FCargo.toml%60.%20The%20build%20therefore%20bypasses%20the%20metadata%20and%20storage%20checks.%20Alias%20resolution%20must%20happen%20before%20applying%20this%20manifest-less%20passthrough%2C%20or%20this%20case%20must%20be%20rejected%20conservatively.%0A%0A**Knowledge%20Base%20Used%3A**%0A-%20%5BCargo%20cache%20integration%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fjdx-org%2F-%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fjdx%2Fmr-boxington%2F-%2Fdocs%2Fcargo-cache-integration.md%29%0A-%20%5BCLI%20and%20configuration%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fjdx-org%2F-%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fjdx%2Fmr-boxington%2F-%2Fdocs%2Fmbx-cli-and-config.md%29%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmr-boxington\u0026pr=481\u0026platform=github\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Fix in Claude Code\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e","id":4031752644,"line":null,"path":"crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs","review":5229475027}
{"body":"### Passthrough skipped for common flags\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\u003e\nThe new no-manifest passthrough sits behind a guard that returns false for `+`, `--config`, `-C`, and `--directory`, so those invocations never reach `manifest_in_scope`. `cargo +nightly binstall` and `cargo -C /tmp binstall` outside a project still hit the storage error this change aims to fix. `manifest_in_scope` already implements `-C`/`--directory` handling, but that logic is unreachable from this caller. The `-Z` part of the guard is the intentional exception for single-file scripts.\n\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 8e2c9c63-f4b5-48a0-a430-b13933e8c625 --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\ncrates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs#L239-L261\ncrates/mbx-cache-cargo/src/lib.rs#L395-L410\nLOCATIONS END --\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eAdditional Locations (1)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n- [`crates/mbx-cache-cargo/src/lib.rs#L395-L410`](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/blob/7add40853f7a6a10b80488e64fd61923bc9661c6/crates/mbx-cache-cargo/src/lib.rs#L395-L410)\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Fix in Web\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\u003csup\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 7add40853f7a6a10b80488e64fd61923bc9661c6. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\u003c/sup\u003e\n","id":4031764150,"line":null,"path":"crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs","review":5229488251}
{"body":"Confirmed and fixed in ac6b5def3, and it turned out to be two holes rather than one.\n\nReproduced with a real `i = \"install\"` alias: `cargo i --path /project` from a manifest-less directory compiled and installed with no mbx involvement. The same command does the same thing on unmodified `main`, so the bypass predates this branch — the alias table re-tested passthrough with `cargo_proxy_passthrough(\u0026[OsString::from(next)])`, the expanded name alone, so `install` looked like a registry install because `--path` was not in that one-element slice.\n\nBoth are closed:\n\n- The alias table now substitutes the expansion into the command line at the subcommand's position and keeps the remaining arguments, so `--path` is still visible when the resolved command is re-tested. `cargo_subcommand_at` reports that position.\n- `manifest_in_scope` no longer looks for a literal `install` before reading `--path`. Any `--path` naming a directory with a `Cargo.toml` counts as a manifest, under whatever spelling of the subcommand, since only Cargo can expand a user's alias.\n\nBoth were needed: the manifest-less check runs first, so fixing the alias table alone still let the invocation through ahead of it.\n\nVerified against the earlier repro — that install is now rejected instead of silently compiling. `an_aliased_path_install_is_still_checked` pins it for `install` and `i`, for both the shim and `mbx cargo`, and a unit case covers `manifest_in_scope`. Literal `install --path .` is still managed by mbx, and `storage_placement` is 15/15.\n\nOne limit worth naming: resolving the roots for an aliased path install needs the alias expanded, which only Cargo can do, so these are rejected conservatively rather than managed — the outcome you suggested as the alternative. Teaching root resolution about aliases is separate work.\n\n_🤖 Addressed by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)_\n","id":4031788190,"line":null,"path":"crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs","review":5229513736}
{"body":"Good catch — fixed in 71c35161e. Confirmed both symptoms against a real Cargo first: `cargo +stable binstall` and a `--config` override outside a project both still hit the storage error.\n\nThe guard mixed two concerns. `+`, `--config`, `-C`, and `--directory` matter only to the `cargo --list` parsing below it, which describes neither the invocation nor its aliases once another Cargo or another configuration is in play. Manifest discovery does not depend on any of them, because no configuration puts a manifest where the filesystem has none. So the manifest check now runs above that guard, with `-Z` kept ahead of it for exactly the reason you identify: a single-file `-Zscript` package compiles without a manifest.\n\n`cargo +stable binstall` and `cargo --config … binstall` outside a project now reach Cargo, and both are pinned in `an_invocation_outside_a_project_still_reaches_cargo`, which asserts the same invocations stay rejected inside a project. The `--config` case is shim-only there, since mbx's own CLI rejects a bare `--config` before this code sees it.\n\nOn `-C` and `--directory`: they are still unreachable, but not because of the ordering. Cargo requires `-Z unstable-options` for `-C`, and `--directory` is not a Cargo flag at all on stable, so those invocations always carry the `-Z` that is deliberately rejected. I left `manifest_in_scope`'s handling of them in place rather than narrowing the `-Z` rule — `-Zscript` is worth more than the convenience, and the helper stays a correct description of where Cargo looks.\n\n`storage_placement` is 15/15, workspace tests pass, and Clippy is clean.\n\n_🤖 Addressed by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)_\n","id":4031809108,"line":null,"path":"crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs","review":5229538688}
{"body":"\u003ca href=\"#\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e **Embedded alias bypasses verification**\n\nWhen a Cargo alias embeds a path install, such as `i = \"install --path /project\"`, invoking `cargo i` outside a project makes this early return inspect only the unexpanded arguments. Cargo then expands the alias and compiles the local package without mbx verifying its build storage. The existing regression test passes `--path` directly on the command line, so it does not cover this form of alias.\n\n**Knowledge Base Used:**\n- [CLI and configuration](https://app.greptile.com/jdx-org/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/jdx/mr-boxington/-/docs/mbx-cli-and-config.md)\n- [Cargo cache integration](https://app.greptile.com/jdx-org/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/jdx/mr-boxington/-/docs/cargo-cache-integration.md)\n\n\u003ca href=\"https://app.greptile.com/ide/claude-code?prompt=This%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20crates%2Fmbx%2Fsrc%2Fcli%2Fshim.rs%0ALine%3A%20255-259%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Embedded%20alias%20bypasses%20verification**%0A%0AWhen%20a%20Cargo%20alias%20embeds%20a%20path%20install%2C%20such%20as%20%60i%20%3D%20%22install%20--path%20%2Fproject%22%60%2C%20invoking%20%60cargo%20i%60%20outside%20a%20project%20makes%20this%20early%20return%20inspect%20only%20the%20unexpanded%20arguments.%20Cargo%20then%20expands%20the%20alias%20and%20compiles%20the%20local%20package%20without%20mbx%20verifying%20its%20build%20storage.%20The%20existing%20regression%20test%20passes%20%60--path%60%20directly%20on%20the%20command%20line%2C%20so%20it%20does%20not%20cover%20this%20form%20of%20alias.%0A%0A**Knowledge%20Base%20Used%3A**%0A-%20%5BCLI%20and%20configuration%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fjdx-org%2F-%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fjdx%2Fmr-boxington%2F-%2Fdocs%2Fmbx-cli-and-config.md%29%0A-%20%5BCargo%20cache%20integration%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fjdx-org%2F-%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fjdx%2Fmr-boxington%2F-%2Fdocs%2Fcargo-cache-integration.md%29%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.\u0026repo=jdx%2Fmr-boxington\u0026pr=481\u0026platform=github\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaudeDark.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Fix in Claude Code\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInClaude.svg?v=7\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e","id":4031821313,"line":null,"path":"crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs","review":5229550965}
{"body":"### Path flag blocks outside-project commands\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\u003e\nTreating any `--path` that names a `Cargo.toml` as a manifest in scope forces those invocations through the in-project metadata-failure path. Installed external subcommands that are not aliases are then rejected, so tools such as `cargo generate --path` fail outside a project with a storage-verification error instead of reaching Cargo. The alias table already distinguishes a path install once it runs; this check prevents every other `--path` user from getting that far.\n\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 62563bdc-d665-4bc4-a125-68a822e68336 --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\ncrates/mbx-cache-cargo/src/lib.rs#L402-L407\ncrates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs#L254-L330\nLOCATIONS END --\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eAdditional Locations (1)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n- [`crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs#L254-L330`](https://github.com/jdx/mr-boxington/blob/71c35161e8dd56a00b5a667fdade339559dedfbc/crates/mbx/src/cli/shim.rs#L254-L330)\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"\u003e\u003c/picture\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cpicture\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"\u003e\u003csource media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com