project. A bare word after a path value was taken as the tail of a value the
listing had split, but a subcommand external to Cargo takes positionals of
its own, and that is an ordinary invocation with nothing to verify.

The word's spelling was never what settled this. Asking the filesystem
whether a longer reading names a real place already answers it, and answers
it in both directions: `--path "/src -x/pkg"` is caught by that alone, and a
trailing crate name is not. So the spelling rule goes, leaving one question
where there were two.

Every alias spelling that must stay refused still is, on the filesystem
check by itself.

